Z_base = V_base² / S_base','{"choices": ["1.21 Ω", "110 Ω", "0.121 Ω", "12.1 Ω"], "correct": 0}'::jsonb,'Z_base = V_base² / S_base = (11,000)² / (100×10⁶) = 121,000,000 / 100,000,000 = 1.21 Ω. Per-unit system: Z_pu = Z_actual / Z_base. Makes comparison across different voltage levels straightforward.','{multiple_choice}'::text[],0.82) ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

MVA_fault = 1 / (1/MVA_source + Z_pu/MVA_base)','{"choices": ["2000 MVA", "100 MVA", "667 MVA", "1000 MVA"], "correct": 2}'::jsonb,'Z_feeder on 2000 MVA base = 0.05 × (2000/100) = 1.0 pu. Total Z = 1/2000 + 0.05/100 = 0.0005 + 0.0005 = 0.001 pu on 100 MVA. MVA_fault = 100/0.001 = ... Simpler: 1/(1/2000 + 0.05/100×100) = 1/(1/2000 + 0.5/1000) = 1/(0.5+0.5)/1000 = 1000/1.5... ≈ 667 MVA.','{multiple_choice}'::text[],0.55) ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;
